 ## Background
-The method originates from the application of Spherical Harmonics to Precomputed Radiance Transfer (PRT) for real-time global illumination [S2, unofficial]. Sloan et al. introduced the use of SH for representing light transport and the rotation of Zonal Harmonics [S2, unofficial]. The specific application to differentiable shadow computation and inverse problems in volume rendering was detailed by [S1] in 2021. Zonal Harmonics were popularized by Sloan et al. (2005) for efficient rotation and projection [S2, unofficial].
